<title>BRAZIL: Brazil insurance watchdog Susep replaces president.</title>
<headline>Brazil insurance watchdog Susep replaces president.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's insurance watchdog Susep has named Helio Portocarrerro, its director, to replace superintendent Marcio Coriolano, who resigned for personal reasons, an agency spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Susep, an arm of the Finance Ministry, is reponsible for supervising and regulating Brazil's insurance and private pension markets.</p>
<p>Currently, Susep is drawing up a regulatory framework for lifting the state's monopoly on the reinsurance market.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415</p>
</text>
